**Lemma 3.4 (direct raw-record inverse).** The actual rooted support of
$U_+(Y)$ determines $Y$'s full raw field values. Its actual terminal
antichain independently determines the same values. This includes every
partly constructed finite version and every raw byte; it requires neither
a valid source tree nor a sealed field.

Proof. Use SSA Theorem 4.4 for each cell and tape. At each fixed $F_q$
socket, a terminal means absent; otherwise the unique fork side distinguishes
the existing zero or one. These three shapes are distinct. This recovers
the construction domain and all finite control, cursor and token bits,
along with every tape track. The marks determine the actual access links.
Every component is a finite full ordered tree, including an absent socket.
SSA.6 therefore recovers its full support from the prefixes of the terminal
paths, and maximal support paths recover the terminals. Apply it to the
whole $U_+$, then the same component decoder. Rooted support does not by
itself guess occurrence names: canonical provenance is recovered in §5.
No extra owner permission is part of this mathematical decoding. ∎

